    "type": "question",
    "label": "79",
    "prompt": "Given a set $X$, its $\\mathit{power\\ set}$, $\\mathcal P(X)$, is the set containing all subsets of $X$. Write down $\\mathcal P(X)$ for\n$$X=\\{p\\}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\mathcal P(X)=\\{\\varnothing,\\{p\\}\\}$",
      "worked": "The subsets are the empty set and $\\{p\\}$. Thus\n$$\\mathcal P(X)=\\{\\varnothing,\\{p\\}\\}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
